Rule 12 (If the input is a list of exactly two integers, the product of its elements must be within safe boundaries)
{v_1 : list(int)} |= if v_1.len = 2 then v_1[0] * v_1[1] ≥ -1000000 ∧ v_1[0] * v_1[1] ≤ 1000000
